{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]Hark! the voice of Jesus [Gb]call[Db]ing,
[Gb]“Who will [Db]go and [Ab7]work [Db]to[Ab]day?
[Db]Fields are white, the harvest [Gb]wait[Db]ing,
[Gb]Who will [Db]bear the [Db]sheaves [Ab7]a [Db]way?”
[Db]Loud and long the [Gb]Mas[Db]ter calleth,
[Db]Rich re[Ab7]ward He [Ebsus]of [Eb7]fers [Ab]free;
[Db]Who will answer, gladly [Gb]say[Db]ing,
[Gb]“Here am [Db]I, O Lord, [Ab7]send [Db]me”?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]If you [Gb]cannot cross [Db]the ocean
[Gb]And [Db]the [Ab7]heathen [Db]lands [Ab]explore,
[Db]You can [Gb]find the [Db]heathen nearer,
[Gb]You [Db]can [Db]help them [Ab7]at [Db]your door;
[Db]If you [Gb]cannot speak [Db]like angels,
[Db]If [Ab7]you [Ebsus]cannot [Eb7]preach [Ab]like Paul,
[Db]You can [Gb]tell the [Db]love of Jesus,
[Gb]You [Db]can say [Ab7]He died [Db]for all.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db]If you [Gb]cannot be [Db]the watchman,
[Gb]Standing [Db]high [Ab7]on [Db]Zion's [Ab]wall,
[Db]Pointing out [Gb]the path [Db]to heaven,
[Gb]Offering [Db]life [Db]and [Ab7]peace [Db]to all;
[Db]With your [Gb]prayers and [Db]with your bounties
[Db]You [Ab7]can [Ebsus]do [Eb7]what [Ab]Heaven demands,
[Db]You can [Gb]be like [Db]faithful Aaron,
[Gb]Holding [Db]up [Ab7]the [Db]prophet's hands.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Db]While the [Gb]souls of [Db]men are dying,
[Gb]And [Db]the [Ab7]Master [Db]calls [Ab]for you,
[Db]Let none [Gb]hear you [Db]idly saying,
[Gb]"There [Db]is [Db]nothing [Ab7]I [Db]can do!"
[Db]Gladly take [Gb]the task [Db]He gives you,
[Db]Let [Ab7]His [Ebsus]work [Eb7]your [Ab]pleasure be;
[Db]Answer [Gb]quickly when [Db]He calleth,
[Gb]"Here [Db]am I, [Ab7]O Lord, [Db]send me."
{end_of_verse}
